    "ovFlow": {
      "fill": "blue",
      "maxH": 900,
      "page": "overview",
      "size": 24,
      "text": "How it works\n\n1. User shares a product link or describes the product, plus a pincode, in ChatGPT.\n2. Our server finds nearby shops; the shop card shows in the chat.\n3. User ticks shops (5 at a time, 'Show 5 more shops'), then taps 'Call 3 shops'.\n4. The same card turns into live call status. Our AI calls; if a shop wants a person, it shows 'Prefers a personal call' so the user can call directly (later: 'Passed to our team').\n5. Results: one row per shop, small call and map icons, tap for price, offers and the recording.\n6. Email with a live status link; 'Open on website' at the bottom of the card.",
      "w": 560,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 300
    },
    "ovRules": {
      "fill": "green",
      "maxH": 900,
      "page": "overview",
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Agreed rules (full list in DESIGN.md)\n\n- Highest Google rating first; shops with fewer than 50 ratings hidden unless too few others.\n- Rating shows count, e.g. ★ 4.6 (1,240).\n- No answer: AI retries once after 5 min.\n- Recording player like a voice note; otherwise 'answer from caller's notes'.\n- Phone's own font; black main button only; green = has it, blue = calling, amber = needs attention, grey = no luck, red = error.\n- Sample data only; nothing built or tested in ChatGPT yet.",
